1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:04,640
The Untapped Therapeutic Frontier There are nine point five million possible drug-disease combinations.

2
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:11,520
You've tested thirty-two thousand five hundred. That's like searching for your keys in zero point three four percent of

3
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:18,480
your house and declaring them lost. The other ninety-nine point seven percent is sitting right there, untested, because

4
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:28,020
paperwork. On Wishonia, when we decided to cure disease, we started by counting two things: how many safe molecules we had,

5
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:34,160
and how many diseases existed. Then we multiplied them. Then we tested them.

6
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:37,980
It took fifty years. We're still not sure why it took so long.

7
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:44,540
Your species has been doing pharmacology for a century. I assumed you'd be further along.

8
00:00:44,860 --> 00:00:53,560
You are not further along. After one hundred years, you have tested approximately one-third of one percent of the drug-disease

9
00:00:53,660 --> 00:00:57,940
combinations you could test using compounds you already know are safe.

10
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:05,880
The rest is sitting there, untested, because testing things costs money and money is currently busy being missiles.

11
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:17,280
Here is the math. It is brief. Your Tiny Sandbox. Here is everything humanity considers "medicine" after five thousand years

12
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:24,460
of civilization: There are twenty thousand prescription products approved in the U.S., which sounds impressive until you

13
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:33,360
realize most are just "Tylenol, but blue." These products contain only one thousand six hundred and fifty unique compounds,

14
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:36,900
which is fewer ingredients than a decent French bakery uses.

15
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:43,040
Seven thousand five hundred investigational drugs have passed Phase One globally.

16
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:51,580
The F.D.A. GRAS list contains six hundred and thirty-five substances that you could eat right now without dying.

17
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:58,240
Total unique compounds humanity knows are safe-ish: nine thousand five hundred compounds.

18
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:03,020
That's it. That's your entire medicine cabinet after five millennia.

19
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:10,840
The Target List (Ways Your Body Breaks). The International Classification of Diseases, or I.C.D.

20
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:14,920
Ten, lists fourteen thousand ways your meat can malfunction.

21
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:20,000
This is your species' most comprehensive to-do list, and you are not doing it.

22
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:25,820
After consolidation, there are one thousand trial-relevant diseases worth actually fixing.

23
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:34,800
The Math You're Ignoring. Take your nine thousand five hundred safe compounds and multiply by one thousand diseases.

24
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:42,140
This gives you the "Combinatorial Space," which is fancy talk for "stuff you could test tomorrow if you weren't busy filling

25
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:51,080
out forms." Nine thousand five hundred compounds times one thousand diseases equals nine point five million plausible drug-condition

26
00:02:51,080 --> 00:03:00,340
combinations. What You've Actually Tested. There are one thousand seven hundred and fifty unique approved drug-disease pairings,

27
00:03:00,780 --> 00:03:08,220
which represents your entire medical canon. Thirty percent of drugs gain at least one new indication after initial approval,

28
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:15,880
while the rest never get a second date. Let's be generous and say you tested ten times as many things that failed (You did.

29
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:22,560
You learned nothing from them.). Total tested: thirty-two thousand five hundred relationships.

30
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:26,860
The Scorecard. Thirty-two thousand five hundred relationships tested divided by nine point five million possibilities equals

31
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:36,840
zero point three four two percent. Humanity has explored about a third of one percent of the theoretically testable drug-disease

32
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:41,840
space. You checked one drawer, closed it, and told the patient the case was cold.

33
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:51,100
The patient is also cold, because the patient is dead. On Wishonia, if someone explored zero point three four percent of

34
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:55,540
something and declared the job finished, we would gently suggest they continue.

35
00:03:56,300 --> 00:04:05,020
On Earth, you publish a paper about the zero point three four percent and apply for a grant to study the remaining zero

36
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:07,480
point three four percent you studied last time. Is The Untested Stuff Useful?

37
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:12,120
You might argue, "Maybe the other ninety-nine point seven percent is useless!".

38
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:20,820
Biology would like a word. Undrugged Targets: Mapping over three hundred and fifty thousand clinical trials showed that

39
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:25,640
only twelve percent of the human interactome has ever been targeted by drugs.

40
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:34,140
You're ignoring eighty-eight percent of your own biology. It's like having a one hundred-room mansion and living exclusively

41
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:43,840
in the bathroom. Polypharmacology: drugs are messy, they hit multiple targets, and F.D.A.-approved drugs often bind to things

42
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:50,840
you didn't intend. This means "side effects" are frequently "cures for something else" that nobody bothered to notice.

43
00:04:51,900 --> 00:05:00,220
Sildenafil was developed for chest pain, it failed, its "side effect" became Viagra, then it got repurposed *again* for

44
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:08,660
pulmonary hypertension. Minoxidil was developed for high blood pressure, its "side effect" was growing hair, and it became

45
00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:15,320
Rogaine. Two drugs, three accidental cures, and zero systematic searches.

46
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:21,310
You keep finding cures by tripping over them in hallways. Imagine if you opened a door on purpose.

47
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:26,780
Network Overlap: Diseases cluster on shared biological networks.

48
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:35,580
Arthritis and Alzheimer's share biological pathways. Lithium was prescribed for gout in the eighteen hundreds; decades later,

49
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:39,240
it turned out to be the gold standard treatment for bipolar disorder.

50
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,600
Nobody connected the dots because nobody was drawing lines between diseases.

51
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:50,620
The drug that treats your grandfather's inflammation might fix your grandmother's neurodegeneration.

52
00:05:51,220 --> 00:05:56,920
You won't find out, because testing it would require paperwork that takes longer than Grandma has left.

53
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:05,780
The Universe is Big. You Are Small. So far we only counted molecules humanity *already has*.

54
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:11,010
The stuff in your cupboards. If you look at what's chemically possible, it gets embarrassing.

55
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:20,420
Chemical Space: there are an estimated ten to the twenty-third power to ten to the sixtieth power drug-like molecules.

56
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:29,080
That's more candidates than there are atoms in your body, or stars in the galaxy, or excuses from your regulatory agencies.

57
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:36,240
Virtual Libraries: ZINC twenty-two contains tens of billions of purchasable virtual molecules.

58
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:45,320
You could order them online, but you haven't. Synthesized: You have made less than ten to the negative fortieth power of

59
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:53,400
possible molecules. Tested divided by possible is approximately ten to the negative twentieth power to ten to the negative

60
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:58,340
fiftieth power. Effectively zero. You haven't even started.

61
00:06:58,940 --> 00:07:06,520
This is like exploring Earth by looking at one grain of sand on one beach in New Jersey, then declaring you've "seen the

62
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:11,240
world." You haven't. You've seen a grain of sand. In New Jersey.

63
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:19,760
Why You Are Still Sick. I want to be very clear about this: you are not sick because curing disease is impossible.

64
00:07:20,260 --> 00:07:27,120
You are sick because you built a system that charges one hundred million dollars to try, and then gave all the money to

65
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:31,030
a different system that builds missiles. The missiles work fine.

66
00:07:31,980 --> 00:07:40,880
Trials Cost Too Much. A typical Phase Two to Three randomized controlled trial, or R.C.T., costs thirty to one hundred million

67
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:44,180
dollars (median cost per patient forty-one thousand dollars).

68
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:49,100
At that price, you only test things pharmaceutical companies can patent.

69
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:57,020
Everything else sits untested. It's a lottery where the ticket costs one hundred million dollars and only rich molecules

70
00:07:57,020 --> 00:08:06,480
are allowed to play. Herd Mentality. Trials overwhelmingly test the same few biological targets due to preferential attachment

71
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:11,980
dynamics. Everyone studies what everyone else studies because that's how you get grants.

72
00:08:12,420 --> 00:08:17,860
It's like if every explorer only went to France because France already had good reviews on TripAdvisor.

73
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:23,140
Meanwhile, undiscovered continents full of cures sit there, undiscovered.

74
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:33,140
No Profit. Most molecules have no patent. No patent means no one hundred million dollar trial, which means no approval.

75
00:08:33,559 --> 00:08:41,400
Metformin, a diabetes drug from the nineteen-fifties, shows persistent signals for reducing cancer risk and extending lifespan.

76
00:08:41,419 --> 00:08:50,480
It costs pennies. It's off-patent. The trial to prove it works for aging (T.A.M.E.) spent years begging for funding because

77
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:54,570
no pharmaceutical company will bankroll a drug they can't monopolize.

78
00:08:54,980 --> 00:08:59,890
The molecule that saves your life has to make money first. If it can't, it won't.

79
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:09,340
You die. Quarterly earnings go up. Neglect. If you have a rare disease with no market, you don't get a drug.

80
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:16,740
Your cells malfunction in an unprofitable way. The invisible hand of the market has weighed your life against quarterly

81
00:09:16,740 --> 00:09:21,420
earnings and found you wanting. Sorry about your death. It was a business decision.

82
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:30,640
How Long to Explore Everything? At the current pace of three thousand three hundred trials per year, how long would it take

83
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:37,320
to systematically test therapeutic possibilities? Tier 1: Single Compounds (Most Conservative).

84
00:09:37,940 --> 00:09:46,620
Testing every known safe compound against every major disease: Nine point five million combinations divided by three thousand

85
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:51,880
three hundred trials per year equals two thousand eight hundred and eighty years.

86
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:58,740
That's almost two thousand eight hundred and eighty years to explore compounds we *already know are safe*.

87
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:02,780
By that math, we won't finish until the year five thousand.

88
00:10:03,660 --> 00:10:11,020
Tier 2: Combination Therapies (Still Defensible). Modern medicine increasingly relies on multi-drug cocktails.

89
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:17,300
Oncology, H.I.V., cardiology, psychiatry: all routinely use drug combinations.

90
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:23,060
So the real question isn't "does this one drug work?" It's "which combinations work?"

91
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:31,280
Testing pairwise combinations of safe compounds: Forty-five point one billion combinations divided by three thousand three

92
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:36,380
hundred trials per year equals thirteen point seven million years.

93
00:10:36,940 --> 00:10:40,310
That's longer than *Homo sapiens* has existed as a species.

94
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:46,110
And that's using only compounds with established safety data, testing only pairs.

95
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:53,640
Not triplets. God help you if you want to try triplets. Tier 3: The Full Chemical Universe (Illustrative).

96
00:10:54,440 --> 00:11:01,960
Beyond known compounds lies the chemical space of ten to the twenty-third power to ten to the sixtieth power drug-like molecules.

97
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:08,780
At current trial capacity, exploring even the *synthesizable* fraction would take longer than the universe has existed.

98
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:14,120
The universe is thirteen point eight billion years old. You need more time than that.

99
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:19,540
To test pills. Pills that already exist. We haven't even started.

100
00:11:20,260 --> 00:11:27,340
But Won't We Run Out of Easy Discoveries? Some will argue "diminishing returns": the more we search, the harder each new

101
00:11:27,340 --> 00:11:31,260
discovery becomes. This assumes we've already picked the low-hanging fruit.

102
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:38,220
You haven't picked *any* fruit. You're standing outside the orchard filling out an application to enter the orchard.

103
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:41,800
The application is forty-seven pages long. The fruit is rotting.

104
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:47,280
Diminishing returns only kicks in after you've explored a significant fraction of the space.

105
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:54,620
At less than one percent explored, every trial teaches you something new about human biology, improving your ability to

106
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:59,280
predict what works next. Learning compounds. Depletion is negligible.

107
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:04,280
You are nowhere near the bottom of the barrel because you have not yet located the barrel.

108
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:11,720
The math: even with weak learning, diminishing returns only matters after exploring about thirty-seven percent of therapeutic

109
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:19,340
space. For combination therapies, that crossover is over five million years away at current pace (thirty-seven percent of

110
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:24,440
forty-five point one billion combinations at three thousand three hundred trials per year).

111
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:28,380
You cannot have diminishing returns when you've barely started looking.

112
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:36,900
See the formal analysis for the equations. The Fix. The Oxford RECOVERY Trial (COVID-19) proved that large-scale pragmatic

113
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:42,060
trials can run for about five hundred dollars and deliver results in less than one hundred days.

114
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:47,520
Five hundred dollars versus forty-one thousand dollars. Read those numbers again.

115
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:55,460
One of them is the reason people are dying. With a decentralized F.D.A., trial capacity increases by twelve point three

116
00:12:55,460 --> 00:13:03,100
times: Nine point five million combinations divided by forty thousand seven hundred trials per year equals two hundred and

117
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:08,200
thirty-four years. Still a long time, but at least it's a number with fewer digits than a phone book.

118
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:14,640
And the first few decades would capture the highest-value discoveries (the low-hanging fruit that current trial scarcity

119
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:17,940
forces you to ignore while people die in the waiting room).

120
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:25,300
More importantly, your decentralized F.D.A. builds *permanent infrastructure* for systematic therapeutic exploration.

121
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:32,220
The goal isn't to "finish." It's to stop leaving cures on the table while you form subcommittees to discuss whether to form

122
00:13:32,220 --> 00:13:35,920
committees to review the proposal to consider them. The Bottom Line.

123
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:43,380
Humanity has empirically tested less than zero point three four two percent of the drug-disease relationships that can be

124
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:50,870
tested using existing safe compounds. If you include the larger chemical universe, humanity has explored roughly one-quadrillionth

125
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:57,110
to one-quintillionth of what is possible (ten to the power of negative twelve to ten to the power of negative fifty).

126
00:13:57,860 --> 00:14:02,160
There are numbers so small that mathematicians get depressed looking at them.

127
00:14:02,340 --> 00:14:08,560
These are those numbers. The overwhelming majority of therapeutic potential remains untouched.

128
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:13,700
Not because cures are impossible. Because trials are too expensive and too slow.

129
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:22,880
A decentralized, automated pragmatic trial system is the only route to systematically explore the remaining ninety-nine

130
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:28,240
point nine nine nine percent of medical space. The cures exist.

131
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:35,240
The molecules are sitting there. The patients are willing. The only thing between them is a system that charges one hundred

132
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:40,820
million dollars to introduce them and takes seventeen years to make the introduction.

133
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:48,660
On Wishonia, this would be considered a hostage situation. On Earth, it is considered "regulation."

134
00:14:49,900 --> 00:14:55,740
Everything you know about medicine is a dot. Everything you could know is the rest of the page.

135
00:14:56,220 --> 00:14:57,700
The dot is not growing.
